On 2026-10-16 07:49, IETF Chair wrote:<br>
&gt; # Last Call Result<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; The IESG received feedback from the community in response to the IETF =
Last Call on the proposed RFC 3683 PR-action for Ken Kubota [1]. After eval=
uating this feedback, the IESG has concluded there is rough consensus to pr=
oceed with the PR-action.<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; Per the terms described in Section 2 of RFC 3683, the administrators o=
f the ietf, tls, sshm, and mod-discuss lists are directed to suspend Ken Ku=
bota=E2=80=99s posting privileges.=C2=A0 Additionally, this same section ad=
vises =E2=80=9Cmaintainers of any IETF mailing list may, at their discretio=
n, also remove posting rights to that IETF mailing list.=E2=80=9D<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; # Highlights from the Community Feedback<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; The IESG thanks the community for providing this feedback and highligh=
ts the following feedback.<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; ## Additional Justification for Action<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; In addition to the messages outlined in [1], the following additional =
message was requested during the IETF Last Call to be added to the record m=
otivating this PR action by the community:<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; * <a href=3D"https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/ietf/OrvxKgjrEOMb95=
KAWoJYSilDxiY/" rel=3D"noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">https://mailarchive.ie=
tf.org/arch/msg/ietf/OrvxKgjrEOMb95KAWoJYSilDxiY/</a><br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; ## Recommendations for PR actions<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; The community made the following recommendations regarding PR actions:=
<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; * Ensuring that the subject of the PR action is directly notified in a=
ddition to using the <a href=3D"mailto:last-call@ietf.org" target=3D"_blank=
">last-call@ietf.org</a> mailing list.<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; * Harmonizing active PR actions with the new RFC 9945-defined procedur=
es.<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; ## Implementing RFC9945<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; The community expressed an urgency to fully implement the procedures o=
f RFC 9945.<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; # Conclusion<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; The IESG reiterates that the purpose of this action is to minimize dis=
ruptive behavior by a single participant.=C2=A0 The IESG also reaffirms tha=
t a diverse set of opinions in the standards process is both important for =
the IETF and actively encouraged.<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; Per RFC 9945, the IETF Moderator Team [2] is authoring the first draft=
 of the new moderation procedures.=C2=A0 For discussion about IETF moderati=
on procedures use <a href=3D"mailto:mod-discuss@ietf.org" target=3D"_blank"=
>mod-discuss@ietf.org</a> [3].<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; Roman Danyliw<br>
&gt; (as IETF Chair, for the IESG)<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; [1] <a href=3D"https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/last-call/JZXmLcV=
